From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NotAlexNoyle <alexnoyle@icloud.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 22:02:16 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] gpu-compositor: a tall band surface for a change that does
 not fit the band surface

cavekit-gpu-rendering.md R8 / T-527. A frame whose change does not fit the 256-row band surface took the
whole path: the frame-sized target (768x1224) cleared, drawn and resolved on the Adreno 220 every frame, and
the read waited for all of it. A 480 px WebGL canvas changes 354-482 rows a frame, so every frame of the
spinning cube went that way (the job ~45 ms, the card 16.6-22.0 fps while the page drew 22-24). A second,
taller band surface (JIHAD_GPU_BAND_TALL rows, default 512, 0 off; its own pbuffer and target, freed with
the context like the band surface's) takes such a frame; frames are packed for the band surface first, so
one that fits it never pays the tall one (desktop Wikipedia's chunked pan frames stay where they were). The
cube's job 15-30 ms; with the daemon's partial invalidation the card shows 25.3-28.0 fps at 480 px.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
